{
  "_comment": "Reply-wire compatibility fixtures (ADR-0130 section 4), decoded by packages/channel-protocol/tests/test_reply_corpus.py through the same TypeAdapter(ReplyEvent) the Discord and mail adapters use. v1_0 holds every 1.0 form exactly as the 1.0-only package serialized it, captured from origin/next at 522dd55eb before 1.1 existed: each must decode and re-serialize to the same bytes, so a 1.0-built adapter keeps accepting everything the platform sends it. v1_1 holds every 1.1 form in the platform's canonical serialization. refused holds bodies every conforming decoder must refuse, each with the error type the Python models raise, a fragment of its message for a cross-field rule, and, under at, the last element of its location where that pins which field refused it. Bytes are compared as compact JSON: separators (',', ':'), keys in the order written here, non-ASCII unescaped.",
